cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hwattest or its evaluation dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "hwattest: open probabilistic hardware-authenticity scoring with reasons"
abstract: >-
  hwattest attaches a probabilistic, privacy-preserving hardware-authenticity
  score to a submission (e.g. a benchmark result): how likely it was produced on
  a real, distinct physical machine rather than a VM, an emulator, a replayed
  trace, or a clone of a machine already seen. Software-only timing and device
  features are measured by a client under a server-issued challenge; a
  self-hostable server scores and clusters. Output is a score with
  human-readable reasons, never a yes/no proof. Ships with a labeled evaluation
  dataset (derived features only, no machine identifiers) and a reproducible
  harness reporting ROC/AUC, false-positive rate on real hardware, a confusion
  matrix, same-machine repeatability, and a public log of known bypasses.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-06"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Scottcjn/hwattest"
